    "regression_hint": "Invariant a correct fix must enforce: no string derived from Commandline's executable or argument fields may reach Runtime.exec()'s implicit \"/bin/sh -c &lt;string&gt;\" (or cmd.exe \"/C &lt;string&gt;\") interpretation while still containing live shell metacharacters (`$(`, backtick, `;`, `|`, `&`, `<`, `>`, `(`, `)`, newline, etc.) \u2014 quoting must either (a) use single-quote wrapping with correct `'` -> `'\\''` escaping for every quoted segment (which fully suppresses expansion in POSIX shells), or (b) reject/escape metacharacters outright rather than merely deciding *whether* to wrap in quotes based on their presence. Regression tests should cover: executable containing `$(...)`/backticks (this POV's variant), executable containing embedded double quotes plus metacharacters (bypassing the \"already quoted\" short-circuit in quoteAndEscape's `startsWith/endsWith` check), an argument containing `$(...)` with isQuotedArgumentsEnabled()==true and ==false, the CmdShell double-quote-wrapping path on Windows (e.g. executable/argument containing `&`, `|`, or a crafted quote sequence exploiting cmd.exe's documented quote-stripping behavior referenced in CmdShell's own Javadoc), and both Commandline.execute() overloads (with and without a working directory) to ensure the fix is applied before either Runtime.exec call, not just one.",
